# Template for `.env`. Copy to `.env` and fill in the values; `.env` is gitignored and this
# is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then edit .env
#
# Nothing loads this automatically, on purpose. A file that is sourced implicitly is a file
# whose contents nobody re-reads. Commands that need it source it for that call only:
#
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# Same convention as the sibling `finkele-axiom` repo.

# Fine-grained Hugging Face token, read-only, for fetching gated public datasets
# (`openspec/changes/second-credit-panel`).
#
# Create at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens with Token type = Fine-grained,
# Preset = Custom, and exactly ONE scope:
#   Repositories > Read contents of public gated repos you can access
#
# Nothing else. In particular NOT:
#   - Jobs > Start and manage Jobs    (this token must not be able to spend money; if we
#                                      later use HF GPU, that gets its own separate token,
#                                      so revoking one does not disturb the other)
#   - any Write scope                 (we never push to HF)
#   - Inference, Billing, Webhooks, Collections, Discussions, Notifications
#   - any Organization permission
#   - any per-repo entry under "Repositories permissions"
#
# Note this differs from finkele-axiom's HF token, which carries Jobs and Write because it
# runs `hf jobs run`. Do not copy those scopes here.
#
# **Scope cannot enforce our licensing boundary.** Hugging Face states that a token always
# has read access to all public repo contents, so no scope prevents pulling TabPFN-family
# weights. `CLAUDE.md` forbids third-party tabular-foundation-model weights entering this
# repository, and that stays a policy rule enforced by review, not by the credential.
# Their published *numbers* are always fine to cite; their checkpoints are not fine to run.
#
# Most public datasets need no token at all, so this may sit unused until a gated one appears.
# Verify with: hf auth whoami
HF_TOKEN=
